note E14 reachability rule (positive): g, never called from the entry f, stores a secret byte in the count
note field. With e14 that store is excused as unreached-from-entry and the scan prints the all-exports
note obligation. Without e14 any DATA store anywhere in the artifact revokes the declaration.
fn g c edit uchar 104 a view uchar 1 to ulong
put c 32 get a 0
if eq get c 32 0
ret 0
end
ret 1
end
fn f c view uchar 104 to ulong
if eq get c 32 0
ret 0
end
ret 1
end
